rst part. Also, on the Thomas Winterton show, if you think my audio sounds like I'm on a bit of an old school radio, I made a proper rookie mistake back in the early days of the podcast. What I'd done was, I had a really good microphone from the get-go. But for about the first seven interviews or eight interviews, if you listen to me in the very first shows, you'll hear my audio doesn't sound great and that's because I plugged the microphone into the laptop but I hadn't connected the actual microphone to be on the settings, the microphone to work and I was still using the laptop audio. You then notice afterwards, all of a sudden the audio improves when I realized what I was doing wrong. It's absolutely fine to listen to and it's only that first interview, it just sounds a little bit old school radio from my side. Thomas Winterton does most of the talking. This is part 1 of the Skinwalker Ranch Omnibus and I hope you enjoy. Part 2 includes interviews again with Brandon Fugal, Eric Bard, Ben Woodruff and Jim Sagala. Sit back, enjoy the Omnibus and I'll speak to you all soon. So welcome back, everyone, to episode 8 of That UFO Podcast. And as I announced a few weeks ago, tonight's guest, I'm very excited to speak to one of the cast, one of the stars of The Curse of Skinwalker Ranch, or The Secret of Skinwalker Ranch, if you're in the USA. It's The Curse of Skinwalker Ranch in the UK. We have Thomas Winterton, Superintendent of the Ranch. Thomas, how are you?

