00:05:37.368 --> 00:07:36.068
<v SPEAKER_2>You know, unfortunately, it really was pretty anticlimactic. I was when I was growing up, there was an old oil refinery that was out on the west side of town. And my window in my bedroom overlooked that. And I was up late. I mean, it was late for a kid. It was probably like 11 or 12 at night. And I looked out the window and I saw this big, gorgeous, beautiful orange moon just out there on the horizon above the refinery. I mean, it looked identical to the moon. But I mean, it was just gorgeous. It was just out there hovering. But it wasn't a full moon. It was like a half moon. But instead of, it was like on its, it was scooped kind of like a bowl, I guess, sitting there on the horizon. And it was big enough and beautiful enough that it definitely caught my attention. I looked at it, I thought, wow. But then I went about my business and I don't remember if I was cleaning up my room or what I was doing. But when I finished, I looked back out the window to see if I could get one more look at the moon before I went to bed. And it wasn't there. And it was low enough on the horizon. Like it was just out there kind of above the refinery, that I just assumed that it had dropped over the horizon. Or, you know, it was just out of sight. And didn't think anything else of it. And the next morning when I got up, I was telling my mom, I got up and I was like, man, you should have saw the moon last night. It was so beautiful. And my mom said, I don't think there was a moon last night. Yeah, there was. I saw it. It was above the refinery. And so we had a calendar, you know, hanging there close and we looked at it. And it was actually that night there was not a moon. So I don't know what I saw out there, hanging above the refinery, but it definitely was not the moon. And that was my first time of seeing an unidentified object. I have no idea what it was, but definitely not scary. It was just big and beautiful and unknown.

00:07:36.908 --> 00:07:43.908
