00:17:18.228 --> 00:19:05.168
<v SPEAKER_2>So I've never even to this day, I've never watched a single one of the documentaries on it. I've never read any of the books. My knowledge of Skinwalker Ranch growing up here was based solely on a lot of the rumors and stories that are going around at church or at school and then in the local newspapers. I haven't seen any of the movies. I haven't read any of the books. And going on to the ranch, my excitement for being able to go on the ranch, and I was excited when Jim offered me the chance because here's this mysterious place that nobody else gets to go on. It was kind of the notoriety, the ability to go do something that most people were not able to. But as far as my personal beliefs in it, you know, the whole paranormal stuff, the skinwalker, all these orbs, all the things have been talked about. I didn't believe in it. I just thought it was people's imaginations running wild. And, you know, part of the problem in the UFO world and the paranormal world is we have a lot of claims and very little evidence to back it up. I'm just supposed to take your word that that hairy thing on your screen is not a dust ball, but rather some type of object up in the sky. So, you know, it's amazing as far as technologically advanced as we are, we still can't seem to get a clear picture of something. You know, they're all grainy and fuzzy. I think you could call me, I was a very healthy skeptic. And I don't, I didn't believe in a lot of it. That was really my viewpoint coming on to the ranch. I had heard the stories. I didn't believe the stories and I didn't think there was anything to it other than just a bunch of imaginations running wild.

