00:20:20.108 --> 00:24:50.108
<v SPEAKER_2>Yeah, so when I met Brandon Fugal for the first time, Jim Morse took me, I drove out to Salt Lake, and Jim Morse took me into Brandon's office. And Brandon, so Brandon is the largest commercial real estate broker in the Intermountain West. He's, his name is everywhere. And you got to understand that for your viewers that are over there, you know, across the pond, the brand and advertise, Brandon is big, he's splashy. He is one of the best salesmen I've ever met in my life as far as he he knows how to present well. So like in his real estate business, when you drive up the between Provo, Utah and Salt Lake, Utah, we call the I-15 corridor because I-15 is the interstate that runs up. Brandon's name, I swear, is like literally on every single building driving up the interstate. And he has been incredibly successful. So I knew Brandon Fugal by name only. I didn't know who he was. All I knew is that every impressive building between Provo and Salt Lake had his name splashed all over the side of it with his phone number. And so this guy must be pretty important. His name's everywhere. And you go to his office and again, his office is incredible. And so for a small town businessman like myself, walking into this new world of these guys that are just operating extremely high level, I love it. I don't get intimidated easy, so I wasn't intimidated at all. But here's a new world I'm being introduced into and Brandon comes in and he spent, I believe our first conversation that day was about three hours long, which for Brandon, he's always going 100 different directions. He's putting out a million fires and I wouldn't be surprised if he's got that superhero cape hidden in the trunk behind the car. I wouldn't be surprised at all. But our first conversation is about three hours and he very meticulously and very clearly communicated with me why he bought the ranch, what his vision was for it, his belief system around it, and then he laid out where he thought that I could assist him in it. We spent three hours together and he's always had a curiosity about the unknown and those life's answers. Are we alone in the universe? Where did we come from? Where are we going? Obviously, we have religious answers to those, but he's really fascinated on the science side, and has put his money where his mouth is. The ranch is not his first endeavor into trying to figure out the unknown. He's invested in tech companies before that were geared around trying to figure this stuff out as well. When he had this opportunity to buy this mysterious ranch where these things are supposedly going on, he jumped on it. Brandon is one of the coolest human beings that I've had the privilege of meeting. When you see him on TV, I read some of the message boards on that, and you hear Brandon in the first episode when he's like, all right, Eric, get the case. You know, he's being like serious. People are like, oh, they're dramatizing this. But those of us that know Brandon Fugal, that is Brandon Fugal. That's not acting. What can I say? He eats his shit up. He loves his stuff. It's what he's grown up in. So that's not Brandon acting. That is really Brandon. He's just a great person to be around. He's very open, very transparent and very caring. I watch people have no idea how much Brandon does for those people around him. He's a very caring human being and he's a good guy. I can't say enough good about Brandon. But his intentions here is purely to get to the bottom of this mystery and try to figure it out and to be very transparent about it. He doesn't have an agenda.

